                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            would categorify to the fusion category of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+spaces"} graded vector spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groups"} 2-groups
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalisation"} internalisation
            of the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
            (which is essentially the same as a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          %p
            In this sense,
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
