            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+bicategories"} monoidal bicategories
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (Terminology)
              There are various names for this particular flavor of fusion category, involving permutations of the words “braided” and “crossed”, or possibly trading “braided” for “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              \-braided”.
            %p
              The latter choice has its justification in the fact that in general, it is
              %em not
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+category"} braided category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              in a crossed module need not be abelian, but up to a group action.
          %h2#definition Definition
